{"companyInfo": {"Updated": "7/28/26", "Footnote": "Market value as of July 13, 2026.", "Country/Territory": "U.S.", "Headquarters": "Minneapolis", "Industry": "Banks: Commercial and Savings", "CEO": "Gunjan  Kedia", "Website": "https://www.usbank.com", "Ticker": "USB", "Company type": "Public", "Revenues ($M)": "$42,861", "Profits ($M)": "$7,570", "Market value ($M)": "$97,109", "Number of employees": "68,520", "StockQuote": "NYSE"}, "description": "\"Founded in 1863, U.S. Bancorp is a comprehensive financial services holding company operating in the United States. The company\u2019s operations are divided into several key segments: wealth, corporate, commercial and institutional banking, consumer and business banking, payment services, and treasury and corporate support. \r\nU.S. Bancorp offers depository services including checking accounts, savings accounts, and time certificate contracts; as well as lending services including traditional credit products, credit card services, lease financing, import/export trade, asset-backed lending, and agricultural finance. U.S. Bancorp\u2019s corporate and institutional services include capital markets, treasury management, and receivable lockbox collection services. In addition, the company offers asset management and fiduciary services for individuals, estates, foundations, business corporations, and charitable organizations. \r\nThe company extends its portfolio with investment and insurance products, primarily within its domestic markets. It also provides fund administration services to mutual and other funds. Corporate and purchasing card services, as well as corporate trust services, are part of U.S. Bancorp\u2019s extensive offerings.\"", "dataTables": [{"changeHeader": "", "footnote": "*Tie in rank.", "title": "World's Most Admired Companies", "valueHeader": "", "values": [{"change": null, "title": "Sector", "value": "Financials"}, {"change": null, "title": "Industry", "value": "Superregional Banks"}, {"change": nul